Same reason as rc-family-type-in-app-argument: this fixture measures the
strong counts a Vec's rc<T> element ownership produces, which is established
at elaboration (RETAIN/BORROW/REJECT classification of the carrier crossing)
and in codegen (`tur-vec-elem-rc?` folded into the -o helpers' `owned` flag).
The interpreter models rc counts but not the emit-time ownership transfer, so
the push/get/pop counts come out one low. Compiled path is green
(bash tests/run.sh).
